5:42Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "As the instructions say for building the passthrough plugin, I first installed MAVSDK and built/tried some of the examples. When I wanted to install the mavlink_passthrough plugin however, I used the command \"make ENABLE_MAVLINK_PASSTHROUGH=1\" in the \".../MAVSDK/build/default\" directory and got no error. However, when looking at the output, I get things like:\r\n\"[ 44%] Built target mavsdk_action\r\n[ 46%] Built target mavsdk_follow_me\r\n[ 48%] Built target mavsdk_geofence\"\r\nwhich seems ok. However, there is no reference to it actually building or doing anything with the mavlink_passthrough plugin. I double checked the \".../build/default/src/plugins/\" and the \"/usr/local/include/mavsdk/plugins/\" directories but again found no mention of the plugin being there. \r\nHow do I build the passthrough plugin to be able to include it in the given example code?", "closed_by": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.g